{q: "initially failed to use the extra free time as he or she had intended?", answer: "B", why: "Ravi chtěl studovat španělštinu atd., ale „For the first month I did none of them“ – den spolkly domácí práce.", evidence: "For the first month I did none of them."},
{q: "mentions tension between different groups of staff?", answer: "C", why: "Mezi kuchyní a obsluhou vznikla „real bad feeling“, protože jen kuchaři dostali volný den. Kate zmiňuje jen reptání („grumbled“), ne napětí mezi skupinami.", evidence: "there was real bad feeling between the kitchen and the dining room"},
{q: "explains why the scheme was dropped?", answer: "C", why: "Rozhodující byla nutnost přijmout tři další lidi, na což marže nestačily: „The final straw was…“. Ostatní u systému zůstali (Ravi: „Would I go back? Absolutely not.“).", evidence: "The final straw was discovering that we'd have to hire three additional staff"},
{q: "questions how reliable some of the evidence is?", answer: "D", why: "Data pocházela z dotazníků samotných účastníků, kteří chtěli, aby to vyšlo – mohli je zkreslit. Ravi kritizuje propagátory, ne data.", evidence: "Much of our data came from questionnaires completed by the participants themselves"},
{q: "believes the timing of the change was a mistake?", answer: "C", why: "Luca: „I chose the worst possible moment to start“ – červenec v turistické sezóně; v lednu by měl čas vychytat problémy.", evidence: "In hindsight, I chose the worst possible moment to start."},
{q: "refers to an expectation that has never been made explicit?", answer: "B", why: "Očekávání stejného výkonu je „never stated, but clearly understood“. Kate mluví o efektivnějším využití času, ale ne o nevyřčeném očekávání.", evidence: "The expectation – never stated, but clearly understood – is that we'll achieve the same output as before"},
{q: "compares the current scheme with an earlier innovation?", answer: "D", why: "Srovnává s pružnou pracovní dobou (flexitime) v 70. letech, která byla přijata se stejným nadšením, ale svět práce nezměnila.", evidence: "In the 1970s, flexitime was greeted with similar enthusiasm"},
{q: "mentions an unforeseen advantage in attracting new staff?", answer: "A", why: "Kate nečekala dopad na nábor: „The benefit I genuinely didn't anticipate was the effect on hiring.“ Luca naopak zjistil, že by musel nabírat – to je nevýhoda.", evidence: "The benefit I genuinely didn't anticipate was the effect on hiring."}
